# ORC Project File
# Version: 2.0
#
# National B, the video stack: the sets selection.yaml chooses for the video,
# in its order, each through a Frame Map and an FM Beat Cancel, all into one
# Source Align, then the Stacker, Dropout Correction, Picture Band Limit and
# the video sink that writes the pack's mkv. build-pack.sh's video stage
# copies this beside its outputs, points each source at its set's decode, sets
# each frame map and the alignment from the committed
# discs/national-b/framemaps/ (made by the map stage), and processes it.
# Nothing here is refreshed, so the stack is built from the reviewed maps.
#
# Each source is labelled with its set id and its frame map "<set> map", as in
# map.orcprj. The sources must be the video sets of selection.yaml, in the
# same order: the first sets the Stacker's sample grid (the compare report's
# suggested reference). Adding or dropping a set means editing this project.
# The Stacker's other settings are Volcanoes' (discs/volcanoes/stack.orcprj
# says why).
#
# The chain follows decode-orc#354's advice, as on National A:
#
# - "<set> beat", FM Beat Cancel, between each frame map and Align: before the
#   Stacker, since the beat's phase differs between masters. The video stage
#   sets each one's carrier_black_mhz from framemaps/<set>.carrier, which the
#   map stage measures.
# - The Stacker is Weighted, with sample_align, still_frame_stacking and
#   pressing_repair: the side's video sets come from four stamper groups
#   (selection.yaml), and the repair replaces a defect every disc of one
#   stamper carries with the stack of the other groups'.
# - No Audio Channel Map vbi_mono_average: the sound is analogue stereo,
#   though the VBI says mono. No Domesday side uses it. audio_stacking stays
#   Mean.
# - Dropout Correction fills dropouts by interpolate, from the clean lines
#   above and below, luma and chroma apart.
# - "Band", Picture Band Limit, after Dropout Correction: it low-passes the
#   luma where the picture ends, the map stage's lumaCutoffMHz
#   (framemaps/picture-band), measured between captures of different stamper
#   families. The video stage sets cutoff_mhz from it; rolloff_mhz stays 0.4.
#   Chroma is untouched.
# - The video sink decodes every frame with transform3d: the side is motion
#   throughout. build-pack.sh sets the decoder from disc.conf, so the two are
#   the same.

project:
  name: National B stack
  version: 2.0
  video_format: PAL
  source_format: Composite
  amplitude_unit: 10bit
dag:
  nodes:
